KG42.register("rules-35f2dae3f5f0a4a30f3763dd",{"id":"10-hierarchical_coordination::v141-c-R011","paper":"10-hierarchical_coordination","record":{"rule_id":"v141-c-R011","mechanism_id":"v141-a-M02","name":"Counterparty matching","process_stage":"matching","market_meaning":"Submitted bidding blocks provide inputs to P2P counterparty matching under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one, using submitted offering and bidding blocks. Submitted offering blocks provide inputs to P2P counterparty matching under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one, using submitted offering and bidding blocks. The LMO coordinates P2P counterparty matching in the local market under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one.","independence_rationale":"Relations governed by the approved function matching.counterparties under the fixed relation-ownership template. Conditional branches retain their explicit scope in local constraints.","V":["bidding.demand","bidding.supply","coordination.local_operator","matching.counterparties"],"E":[{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E001","source":"bidding.demand","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e36"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E002","source":"bidding.supply","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e36"]},{"edge_id":"v141-c-R011-E003","source":"coordination.local_operator","target":"matching.counterparties","type":"links","constraint_ids":["v141-c-R011-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e24"]}],"omega":{"market_type":"LEM","network_level":null,"jurisdiction":null,"pricing_scope":null,"time_scale":null,"participant_types":[],"trading_stage":"matching","context_text":"First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one, using submitted offering and bidding blocks. | First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one.","unknown_fields":["network_level","jurisdiction","pricing_scope","time_scale","participant_types"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e24","v141-b-g02-e36"]},"x":[{"variable_id":"v141-c-R011-x1","symbol":"P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm}","meaning":"Quantity of offering block for P2P trading allocated from prosumer j to prosumer i at time slot t and block m under strategy one. Source Eq. (20) bounds it below by 0 and above by the submitted offering quantity O_{jtm}. The source definition does not state a unit; example values in the case study are reported in kWh.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real quantity, bounded above by O_{jtm} according to source Eq. (20)","unit":null,"indices":["j","i","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"variable_id":"v141-c-R011-x2","symbol":"P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm}","meaning":"Quantity of bidding block for P2P trading allocated from prosumer i to prosumer j (equivalently, j's bidding block matched against i) at time slot t and block m under strategy one. Source Eq. (21) bounds it below by 0 and above by the submitted bidding quantity B_{jtm}. The source definition does not state a unit; example values in the case study are reported in kWh.","kind":"operational","domain":"nonnegative real quantity, bounded above by B_{jtm} according to source Eq. (21)","unit":null,"indices":["j","i","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]}],"theta":[{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R011-t1","symbol":"O_{jtm}","meaning":"Offering quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t. It is an output of the prosumer bidding strategy and a submitted input to the LMO's strategy-one matching problem (source Eq. (20)).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R011-t2","symbol":"B_{jtm}","meaning":"Bidding quantity of prosumer j in block m and time t. It is an output of the prosumer bidding strategy and a submitted input to the LMO's strategy-one matching problem (source Eq. (21)).","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R011-t3","symbol":"\\lambda^{o}_{jtm}","meaning":"Offering price of prosumer j in block m and time t, an output of the prosumer bidding strategy used in the strategy-one matching objective (source Eq. (24)). The source definition does not state a unit; case-study costs are reported in cents.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["j","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"parameter_id":"v141-c-R011-t4","symbol":"\\lambda^{b}_{itm}","meaning":"Bidding price as printed in the strategy-one matching objective Eq. (24). The surrounding source text says offering and bidding prices are outputs of the bidding strategy problem for prosumer j, but Eq. (24) prints the bidding price with index i (counterparty) instead of j; the exact intended index is unresolved and the expression is transcribed as printed. The nomenclature separately defines \\lambda^{b}_{jtm} as the bidding price of prosumer j in block m and time t.","value":{"kind":"unspecified","number_value":null,"text_value":null},"unit":null,"indices":["i","t","m"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]}],"phi":[{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C001","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted bidding blocks provide inputs to P2P counterparty matching under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one, using submitted offering and bidding blocks.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C002","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"Submitted offering blocks provide inputs to P2P counterparty matching under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one, using submitted offering and bidding blocks.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e20","v141-b-g02-e36"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C003","kind":"procedural","role":"core","statement":"The LMO coordinates P2P counterparty matching in the local market under strategy one. Scope: First-stage local P2P market under LMO coordinating strategy one.","expression":null,"formalization_origin":"not_formalized","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":[],"parameter_refs":[],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g02-e02","v141-b-g02-e24"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C004","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under coordinating strategy one, the P2P bidding block quantity allocated to a matched ordered pair (j,i) is bounded below by zero and above by prosumer j's submitted bidding quantity B_{jtm}, for each ordered pair of distinct prosumers, each block m and each time t (source Eq. (21)).","expression":"0 \\leq P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} \\leq B_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t \\qquad (21)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.demand","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x2"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-t2"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C005","kind":"mathematical","role":"core","statement":"Under coordinating strategy one, the P2P offering block quantity allocated to a matched ordered pair (j,i) is bounded below by zero and above by prosumer j's submitted offering quantity O_{jtm}, for each ordered pair of distinct prosumers, each block m and each time t (source Eq. (20)).","expression":"0 \\leq P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} \\leq O_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t \\qquad (20)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x1"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-t1"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g02-e18","v141-b-g02-e20"]},{"constraint_id":"v141-c-R011-C006","kind":"mathematical","role":"supporting","statement":"Under coordinating strategy one, the LMO's matching of submitted offering and bidding blocks is expressed by the objective function OF^{1}, which sums over time, blocks and ordered distinct prosumer pairs the offer-price-weighted allocated offering block minus the bid-price-weighted allocated bidding block (source Eq. (24)); the source states the corresponding LMO problem as min OF^{1} subject to (16)-(23).","expression":"OF^{1} = \\sum_{jtm} \\sum_{i(i \\neq j)} (\\lambda^{o}_{jtm} P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} - \\lambda^{b}_{itm} P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm}) \\qquad (24)","formalization_origin":"source","template_id":null,"members":["coordination.local_operator","matching.counterparties","bidding.supply","bidding.demand"],"variable_refs":["v141-c-R011-x1","v141-c-R011-x2"],"parameter_refs":["v141-c-R011-t3","v141-c-R011-t4"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e20","v141-b-g02-e20"]}],"pi":[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p04-c1r2__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":4,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1. First stage: P2P energy market","anchor_text":"Fig. 1. Players and our proposed framework for e 2.1. First stage: P2P energy market LE 𝜆−𝑡 In the f","equation_id":null,"figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-04.png","occurrence_role":"definition"},"source_text":"Although the LMO is in charge of coordinating P2P matches in the local market, each P2P energy trading has its corresponding matching price which does not depend on the rest of P2P transactions in the LEM."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e20","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.2. P2P coordinating problem","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 302 (2021) 117575 to where 𝑃𝑝2𝑝,+,𝑏𝑙𝑗𝑖𝑡𝑚 and 𝑃𝑝2𝑝,−,𝑏𝑙𝑗𝑖𝑡, express the quantity of of","equation_id":"(24)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this paper, we propose two coordinating strategies for P2P energy trading in the LEM. In strategy one, \\Upsilon^{1}, the LMO coordinates the P2P energy transactions locally to maximize matching the offering and bidding blocks submitted by prosumers as presented in (24): OF^{1} = \\sum_{jtm} \\sum_{i(i \\neq j)} (\\lambda^{o}_{jtm} P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} - \\lambda^{b}_{itm} P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm}),   (24) where \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} and \\lambda^{b}_{itm} present offering and bidding prices for P2P trading between prosumers j and i at time t and block m which are outputs of bidding strategy problem for prosumer j. Moreover, it is noted that \\lambda^{o}_{jtm} (\\lambda^{b}_{jtm}) are different with \\lambda^{lm}_{jt\\omega} which is an input of bidding strategy problem for prosumer j."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c2r3__v141-a-M02-pricing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.2. P2P coordinating problem","anchor_text":"of ∑ ∑ 𝑂𝐹2 = 𝑃𝑝2𝑝,+𝑗𝑖𝑡 , (25)ng 𝑗 𝑖(𝑖≠𝑗)𝑡 it ne here, the P2P coordinating problem for strategy two ","equation_id":"(26)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"In this way, after the LMO matches P2P energy trading between prosumers i and j, their P2P trading price is obtained in Eq. (26): \\lambda^{p2p}_{jit} = (\\lambda^{o}_{jt} + \\lambda^{b}_{it}) / 2, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall t   (26) where \\lambda^{p2p}_{jit} represents the price of P2P energy trading between prosumers j and i."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e36","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p07-c2r3__v141-a-M02-matching","page":7,"printed_page":null,"section":"3.2. Evaluation of P2P coordinating strategies","anchor_text":"ids for P2P trading based on strategy one at t = 12. and bids of prosumers in strategy one at 𝑡= 12.","equation_id":null,"figure_id":"Fig. 6","table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-07.png","occurrence_role":"example"},"source_text":"Fig. 6 illustrates an example of P2P matching based on submitted offers and bids of prosumers in strategy one at t = 12. Figs. 6(a) and (b) show all offers and bids submitted by prosumers and consumers at t = 12. ... As mentioned before, the main purpose of strategy one is to minimize difference between offers and bids of prosumers. Hence, P2P trading between P3 and P9 is matched as shown in Fig. 6(a), where the quantity of their traded P2P is 0.384 kWh. Then, the rest of offered energy by P3, 0.157 kWh, is traded with P10."},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"5","section":"2.1.2. P2P coordinating problem","anchor_text":"𝑗 where 𝑃𝑗and 𝐿𝑗represent maximum energy generation (PV capacity) and consumption for prosumer 𝑗. Be","equation_id":"(20),(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"0 \\leq P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} \\leq O_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t \\qquad (20)\n0 \\leq P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} \\leq B_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t \\qquad (21)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g01-e20","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c2r1__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":"5","section":"2.1.2. P2P coordinating problem","anchor_text":"Applied Energy 302 (2021) 117575 to where 𝑃𝑝2𝑝,+,𝑏𝑙𝑗𝑖𝑡𝑚 and 𝑃𝑝2𝑝,−,𝑏𝑙𝑗𝑖𝑡, express the quantity of of","equation_id":"(24)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"formula"},"source_text":"OF^{1} = \\sum_{jtm} \\sum_{i(i \\neq j)} (\\lambda^{o}_{jtm} P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} - \\lambda^{b}_{itm} P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm}), \\qquad (24)"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e18","location":{"location_id":"src-87ebdce2a6-p05-c1r4__v141-a-M02-clearing","page":5,"printed_page":null,"section":"2.1.2. P2P coordinating problem","anchor_text":"𝑗 where 𝑃𝑗and 𝐿𝑗represent maximum energy generation (PV capacity) and consumption for prosumer 𝑗. Be","equation_id":"(20)-(21)","figure_id":null,"table_id":null,"image_ref":"pages/page-05.png","occurrence_role":"condition"},"source_text":"Eqs. (20) and (21) represent maximum and minimum constraints of P2P energy blocks: 0 \\leq P^{p2p,+,bl}_{jitm} \\leq O_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t   (20)   0 \\leq P^{p2p,-,bl}_{jitm} \\leq B_{jtm}, \\forall j, j \\neq i, \\forall m, \\forall t   (21)"}],"field_notes":{"empty_E_reason":null,"empty_x_reason":null,"empty_theta_reason":null},"evidence_basis":"explicit","implementation_status":"unimplemented","status":"needs_review","lead_ids":["v141-a-M02-clearing","v141-a-M02-matching","v141-a-M02-pricing","v141-a-M03-pricing"],"extras":{"decision_anchor":"matching.counterparties","graph_fact_supports":[[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e20","quote":"the LMO coordinates the P2P energy transactions locally to maximize matching the offering and bidding blocks submitted by prosumers"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e36","quote":"Fig. 6 illustrates an example of P2P matching based on submitted offers and bids of prosumers in strategy one at t = 12."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e20","quote":"the LMO coordinates the P2P energy transactions locally to maximize matching the offering and bidding blocks submitted by prosumers"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e36","quote":"Fig. 6 illustrates an example of P2P matching based on submitted offers and bids of prosumers in strategy one at t = 12."}],[{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e02","quote":"the LMO is in charge of coordinating P2P matches in the local market"},{"evidence_id":"v141-b-g02-e24","quote":"the LMO matches P2P energy trading between prosumers i and j"}]],"C2_formalization":{"graph_sha256":"4a69b64858e743a7e1430c7f021f3a2f6df8f030d3f27c74bf862c60ba422854","applicability":"needs_revision","reason":"The original C.1 constraints for this rule are procedural data-flow/coordination statements: submitted bidding and offering blocks feed the LMO's P2P counterparty matching, and the LMO coordinates that matching. The source also contains mathematical content for strategy-one matching: the allocated offering and bidding block quantities are bounded by the submitted offering and bidding quantities (Eqs. (20)-(21)), and the LMO's matching coordination is expressed by objective Eq. (24), with the source stating min OF^{1} s.t. (16)-(23). However, the frozen graph V for this rule lacks clearing.local and the variable-level nodes used by the strategy-one allocation constraints (16)-(19), (22)-(23); therefore the full matching optimization cannot be faithfully transcribed here without either moving R009's clearing facts or adding nodes/edges. Partial formalization is provided under the existing nodes as C004 (Eq. (21) bound), C005 (Eq. (20) bound) and C006 (Eq. (24) objective). The original C001-C003 remain not_formalized because their full mathematical implementation (the LMO strategy-one optimization problem) is not representable in the frozen graph. The source's Eq. (24) also prints a bidding-price index i that conflicts with the nomenclature's lambda^b_{jtm}; this uncertainty is retained. Precise C.1 requests are listed.","bindings":[{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-x1","node_ids":["matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"x1 is the strategy-one P2P offering block allocation variable for matched ordered pair (j,i). It is the matching outcome at matching.counterparties and is bounded by the submitted offering quantity O_{jtm} that arrives from bidding.supply through edge E002."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-x2","node_ids":["matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"x2 is the strategy-one P2P bidding block allocation variable for matched ordered pair (j,i). It is the matching outcome at matching.counterparties and is bounded by the submitted bidding quantity B_{jtm} that arrives from bidding.demand through edge E001."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-t1","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"O_{jtm} is the offering quantity submitted by prosumer j in block m/time t. It is carried by edge E002 from bidding.supply into matching.counterparties as an input parameter to the matching bounds."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-t2","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"B_{jtm} is the bidding quantity submitted by prosumer j in block m/time t. It is carried by edge E001 from bidding.demand into matching.counterparties as an input parameter to the matching bounds."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-t3","node_ids":["bidding.supply"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"lambda^o_{jtm} is the offering price submitted with prosumer j's offering blocks. It travels along edge E002 from bidding.supply to matching.counterparties and weights the allocated offering blocks in Eq. (24)."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-t4","node_ids":["bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"lambda^b_{itm} is the bidding price appearing in the strategy-one objective Eq. (24). It travels along edge E001 from bidding.demand to matching.counterparties and weights allocated bidding blocks. The printed index i (counterparty) conflicts with the source nomenclature lambda^b_{jtm}; this uncertainty is retained."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C004","node_ids":["bidding.demand","matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E001"],"rationale":"C004 formalizes source bound Eq. (21), the mathematical content of the relation that submitted bidding blocks provide inputs to matching: the matched bidding block allocation at matching.counterparties is bounded above by the bidding quantity B_{jtm} arriving via edge E001 from bidding.demand."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C005","node_ids":["bidding.supply","matching.counterparties"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"C005 formalizes source bound Eq. (20), the mathematical content of the relation that submitted offering blocks provide inputs to matching: the matched offering block allocation at matching.counterparties is bounded above by the offering quantity O_{jtm} arriving via edge E002 from bidding.supply."},{"object_id":"v141-c-R011-C006","node_ids":["coordination.local_operator","matching.counterparties","bidding.supply","bidding.demand"],"edge_ids":["v141-c-R011-E003","v141-c-R011-E001","v141-c-R011-E002"],"rationale":"C006 transcribes source objective Eq. (24). The LMO (coordination.local_operator) coordinates matching (edge E003 to matching.counterparties) by weighting allocated offering/bidding blocks with the submitted offering/bidding prices that arrive through edges E002 (bidding.supply) and E001 (bidding.demand)."}],"revision_requests":["Please clarify whether v141-c-R011 is intended to carry the mathematical strategy-one matching optimization or only the procedural data-flow/coordination relation. The source states the LMO coordination problem as min OF^{1} s.t. (16)-(23) (evidence v141-b-g01-e21, v141-b-g02-e21). The frozen V lacks clearing.local and the variables/constraints (16)-(19), (22)-(23); if the rule is meant to be mathematical, add clearing.local and the missing variable/constraint nodes/edges, or confirm that the mathematical clearing content remains exclusively with v141-c-R009 and that R011 stays procedural.","The printed strategy-one objective (24) uses lambda^b_{itm} (counterparty index i) while the nomenclature and surrounding text describe lambda^b_{jtm} (prosumer j). Please obtain a B re-extraction or author clarification on the intended index before treating the objective as fully faithful.","For the block bounds Eqs. (20)-(21), the edges from bidding.supply/bidding.demand to matching.counterparties are typed 'links' in the frozen graph. If these bounds are to be attached as core constraints, consider whether a 'limits' edge type is needed; currently they are added as mathematical constraints under the existing links edges.","The source matching example (Fig. 6, evidence v141-b-g02-e36) identifies matched counterparties P3-P9 and P3-P10 and quantities 0.384 kWh and 0.157 kWh, but no individual-agent nodes exist in V; confirm whether such example instantiations should be represented as instances or left as evidence-only."]}},"quarantined_references":[]}});
